@startuml qnx_dispatch_engine_register_endpoint_activity
title QnxDispatchEngine - client endpoint registration

start
:Enter RegisterPosixEndpoint(endpoint)\nAssert IsOnCallbackThread();
:Grow the client receive buffer if needed\nto endpoint.max_receive_size + 1;
:Append the borrowed endpoint to posix_endpoint_list_;
:Find the first poll slot whose endpoint is nullptr;
if (A free slot exists?) then (reuse)
    :Store the endpoint pointer in that slot\nand increment its nonce;
else (append)
    :Use poll_endpoints_.size() as the new index;
    if (Index equals UINT32_MAX?) then (yes)
        :Return without a poll slot or native registration\nThe intrusive endpoint membership remains;
        stop
    else (available index)
        :Append a poll slot with this endpoint and nonce 0;
    endif
endif

:Build the private sticky-select request\nwith new-data and ping events;
:Iterate the two local signal/event pairs;
while (Another event pair?) is (yes)
    :Pack index, signal and nonce into the pulse value;
    :Initialize the event for the client side channel\nwith kSelectPulseCode;
    :MsgRegisterEvent(event, endpoint.fd);
    if (Registration fails?) then (yes)
        :Log the MsgRegisterEvent error;
    else (registered)
        :Continue without an error log;
    endif
endwhile (no)
:MsgSend the request containing both events to endpoint.fd;
if (MsgSend fails?) then (yes)
    :Log the MsgSend error;
else (sent)
    :Continue without an error log;
endif
:Return without a status or registration rollback;
stop

legend
    The context assertion accepts either engine worker, not arbitrary callers.
    Registration does not reschedule itself or close the descriptor.
    The engine borrows endpoint storage and owns only list/slot membership.
    Event-registration failures are logged, but both events and MsgSend
    are still attempted and local registration state is retained.
endlegend

@enduml
